// REJECTED — `%` (and the named `div_*` / `mod`) stay Int-only for now. The
// remainder is width-agnostic in value, but its zero-divisor *fault* is not
// uniform once Int32 is a `number` on the TypeScript tier and an i32 on wasm.
// Rather than ship a `%` whose fault diverges, revl asks you to widen the
// Int32 operands with `.to_int()` first (docs/arithmetic.md).
//
// expected error:
//   `%` is Int-only; widen the Int32 operands with `.to_int()` first

fn rem(a: Int32, b: Int32) -> Int {
  return a % b
}
